# Owner activation-funnel lens (Issue #648 / docs/PRODUCT_ACTIVATION_FUNNEL.md): the owner-only, content-free
# aggregate view of how far live installations get down the activation path + the founder-report screen the
# weekly GTM review reads. One gate per file. GATE-HYGIENE: description strings must contain NO dollar-sign and
# NO backtick (they are sourced by bash).
register_gate "tests/test_owner_activation_funnel_surface.py" "OWNER-ACTIVATION-FUNNEL GATE: PASS" "owner activation-funnel surface: cross-tenant content-free A1..A9 funnel counts, owner-only, zeros when dormant" "owner activation-funnel surface (Issue 648): core.owner_activation_funnel_surface() is the weekly-GTM-review lens over how far live installations get down the activation path (install -> selected a repo A2 -> first eligible PR traffic A3 -> first PR check published A4 -> first non-Clear signal A5 -> repeat use within 7 days A9) — the SAME owner-only cross-tenant model + lock as owner_cost_surface / owner_compat_shadow_surface (live tenants enumerated via the no-RLS installation_account routing map, each pinned + read inside its own FORCE-RLS wall, REVOKE-PUBLIC / GRANT-veripsa_app), a pure READ over the existing installation_account / claim / event / repository_lifecycle_activation tables (no new table). READ-ONLY reporting: it never changes the write gate, webhook routing, or any runtime decision. Every claim/event/activation read is fenced by the repository generation boundary + excludes unsuperseded lifecycle tombstones, exactly as repos_for_installation, so uninstall/reinstall + repo delete/recreate cannot corrupt the counts. STRICTLY AGGREGATE output: A1 install/live totals + owner-vs-external split (dev-exempt allowlist), A2/A3/A4/A5/A9 stage counts, the warn-vs-serialize signal split, the A1->A3 install-to-first-PR latency aggregate (content-free seconds), the A4 first-PR-check-published count with its first-check signal split and its install-to-check and first-PR-to-check latency aggregates (DB-derivable from the append-only check_published event, not a new table), and the A6/A7/A8 GitHub-only NULL sentinels (never fabricated), plus the bound-honesty fields (account_count/capped/cap/accounts_scanned; at most p_cap accounts visited per call). NO repo names, NO paths, NO branches, NO SHAs, NO PR numbers ever appear. Rendered by github-app/activation_report.py as the owner-DSN-authenticated founder screen, independently guarded so an undeployed surface renders a clean one-line message and never crashes. Proven on a real three-tenant database (two external + one dev-exempt owner) with traffic recorded through the REAL recorders declare_claim_with_authority / record_warn_with_authority / record_collision_with_authority / record_check_published_with_authority: zeros + null timestamps when dormant; exact A1 split + A2/A3/A5/A9 counts + warn/serialize split + latency aggregate + GitHub-only NULL sentinels; A4 first-check increments + latency + signal buckets, a same-head redelivery dedups to one count, and a stale-generation publish is excluded exactly as A3/A5; poison repos/paths/PR-numbers/head-SHAs absent from the serialized output and the rendered text; a buyer/tenant role refused EXECUTE; p_cap=1 flags the top-cap view honestly while keeping the A1 totals exact; the renderer never raises." "owner activation-funnel surface: dormant funnel reads as zeros, A1 split + A2/A3/A5/A9 counts + signal split + latency exact, A4 first-PR-check DB-derivable (increments, latency, signal buckets, same-head dedup, stale-generation excluded), A6/A7/A8 stages returned as NULL sentinels not fabricated, output strictly aggregate with zero repo/path/PR/SHA leakage, buyer role refused, p_cap bound honest with A1 totals exact, activation_report renderer never raises. Gate 251." 20 420
